WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.087
Let’s walk through RFIs.

00:00:02.087 --> 00:00:04.375
Use an RFI when the team needs a ruling,

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:07.250
clarification, or missing scenario fact.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.675
State one decision-blocking question with enough context to answer,

00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:13.650
and revise the same record if White Cell returns it

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:13.775
.

00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:16.312
On this slide, read the team’s questions to White

00:00:16.312 --> 00:00:18.462
Cell and their revision status.

00:00:18.462 --> 00:00:22.175
In practice, a returned RFI remains the same record

00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:25.225
and shows what clarification is still required.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.875
When you are ready, use Open RFIs to move

00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:29.288
to the live surface.

00:00:29.785 --> 00:00:32.460
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:32.635
.
